The plain-text alternative of the banded fixture.

The HTML part is the other half of real newsletter markup: full-width coloured
bands, each wrapping a 600px column. The bands must keep spanning the pane at
every width, including the widths at which the column inside them reflows.

--alt-0012
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

<html>
  <head>
    <title>Banded newsletter</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin:0;padding:0;">
    <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#16598d;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding:18px;">
          <table width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:600px;">
            <tr>
              <td style="font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#ffffff;font-size:20px;">
                A band that must span the pane
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#ffffff;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding:18px;">
          <table width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:600px;">
            <tr>
              <td style="font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  Each coloured strip here is a <code>&lt;table width="100%"&gt;</code> with a
                  background, wrapping a 600px column. It is the other half of how real newsletters
                  are built, and the half a reflow can quietly break: clear a table's own width and
                  the strip shrinks to its contents, so the colour stops reaching the edges while
                  the text inside it still looks right.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0;">
                  So the bands are the assertion. At every pane width, narrow enough to reflow the
                  column or wide enough to leave it alone, all three strips run edge to edge.
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#f0a500;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding:18px;">
          <table width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:600px;">
            <tr>
              <td width="200" style="font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;">First of three</td>
              <td width="200" style="font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Second of three</td>
              <td width="200" style="font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;">Third of three</td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>

--alt-0012--
